00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:00.640
In 1946, right after the end of the war,

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:02.940
<b>Host
Sakai Masato</b>

00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:05.980
a certain novelist's ideas came as a shock to the Japanese.

00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:06.980
His name is Sakaguchi Ango.
Cherry Blossoms   in Full Bloom
In the Woods Beneath the

00:00:06.980 --> 00:00:08.980
<b>Photo: Shigeru Tamura
Ango Sakaguchi</b>

00:00:08.980 --> 00:00:09.820
In his "On Decadence", he
advocated an original way of thinking:

00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:12.860
On Decadence

00:00:13.450 --> 00:00:14.950
To live, to become decadent.

00:00:14.950 --> 00:00:18.780
People need to properly fall down the path of decadence.

00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:24.330
By doing this, they will discover themselves and shall be saved.

00:00:24.330 --> 00:00:26.830
Ango denied the various authorities that the pre-war Japanese believed in.

00:00:26.830 --> 00:00:28.790
denied the authorities

00:00:28.790 --> 00:00:31.800
He preached that people should live like humans

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:32.170
by saying you like what you like and hate what you hate.

00:00:32.170 --> 00:00:35.300
live like humans
by saying you like what you like and hate what you hate.

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:38.850
And Ango expressed his original thinking regarding the cherry blossoms, which the Japanese love beyond all else,

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:39.680
Cherry Blossoms

00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:44.770
in his, <i>In the Woods Beneath the Cherry Blossoms in Full Bloom</i>.
